  "solution": {
    "text": "Domain of $f(x)=\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{x-1}{2 x+3}\\right)$ is\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& 2 x+3 \\neq 0 \\& x \\neq \\frac{-3}{2} \\text { and }\\left|\\frac{(x-1)}{2 x+3}\\right| \\leq 1 \\\\\n& |x-1| \\leq|2 x+3|\n\\end{aligned}$\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/OkE4iMeQTtMyxIVV_CzlE2otwc_q_uu2dNbLNcCRc8E.original.fullsize.png\"><br />$\\begin{aligned} & \\text { For }|2 x+3| \\geq|x-1| \\\\ & x \\in(-\\infty,-4] \\cup\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}, \\infty\\right) \\\\ & \\alpha=-4 \\& \\beta=-\\frac{2}{3}: 12 \\alpha \\beta=32\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
